# An example `.paja/models` for a smaller Claude plan. Copy it to `.paja/models` on your
# default branch to use it; Paja reads that file from the default branch, never from a branch
# under review. Paja's own file runs build and fix on sonnet, review on opus, and gives
# build and fix 80 turns; see docs/usage.md for what each line costs.

# Building and fixing are most of the spend, so they run on the cheaper model.
build sonnet
fix haiku
# The first full review reads the whole change, so it keeps a model that catches mistakes.
review sonnet
re-review haiku
review-2 haiku
triage haiku
plan haiku
# A model to use when the chosen one is busy.
fallback haiku

# Fewer turns per session: a session that hits its cap stops and the next round continues.
max-turns build 50
max-turns fix 40
max-turns review 20
max-turns re-review 15
max-turns review-2 15
max-turns plan 10

# Start no build once this share of the usage window is used (default 90).
window 80
